# packages/core conventions

`packages/core` is **pure domain logic + all domain types**. This is what React
Native reuses later, so it has **ZERO platform / UI / DB dependencies** — no
`pg`, no React, no Next, no browser/Node-only APIs. If you reach for one, the
code belongs elsewhere.

## Types are owned here
- **All domain types live once** in `src/types.ts`. Everything else imports them; never redeclare a domain shape (DRY).
- The DB schema (`packages/db/src/schema.ts`) mirrors these types — when a type changes, the schema must follow (see `/db-migrate`).

## Calculations
- 1RM, plates, volume, progression live in `src/calc.ts` — pure functions, no side effects.
- **Add a colocated `*.test.ts` for every new pure function.** Follow `calc.test.ts`'s house style: table-driven cases, exact expected numbers, edge/boundary inputs (zero, negative, empty, rounding seams). These are the fast gate (`pnpm --filter @rackd/core test`).
- Stored/asserted weight is canonical **kg** — assert in kg, never lb.

## Timer
- `src/timer.ts` is wall-clock: store an absolute `endAt`, recompute `remainingMs(state, now)`. **Always inject `now`** into functions and tests — never call `Date.now()` inside the logic or assert against real wall-clock time.

## Discipline
- **KISS** — no server/AI/abstraction until a real second caller exists. Rule of three before extracting.

See `@AGENTS.md` for global rules and commands.
